  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   We propose an optimization strategy combining:\n   a) Progressive structure learning - start from a known pattern and evolve toward more optimal configurations\n   b) Multi-resolution patching - apply dynamic interpolation to explore higher resolution regions\n   c) Discretized time-delay embedding - use simulated lag embeddings to handle shifted correlations\n   The key insight is that while local search might find improvements in the given parent solution, we need a skeleton that allows jumping out of local minima while respecting the global structure. The repair mechanism will prioritize symmetry and energy-conserving transitions to maintain the integral constraint.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   Representation: Discrete vector h of length n_points satisfying:\n     0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n     sum(h) = n_points/4 (since dx=2/n_points, integral=0.5)\n   Objective: Minimize max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx over integer lags k\n   Processing:\n     h_double = vec([h, reverse(h)])\n     corr_vec = correlate(h_double, 1-h_double, mode='full') * dx\n     C5 = max(corr_vec)\n\n   Algorithm:\n     Use a wrapped Simulated Annealing (SA) with:\n       - Dynamic cooling schedule: T initial=0.1, T final=0.01\n       - Progressive deformation: a. Search local neighbor basins via BFGS\n                            b. If stuck, insert interpolated patches from known structures\n     Transition scaling: Pareto-optimal scaling between structural preservation (\u03bb=0.8) and energy reduction (\u03bb=0.2)\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   Step 1: Validate inputs\n      - Ensure repair weights are positive\n      - Compute center and target_sum = n_points/4\n\n   Step 2: Initial exploration\n      h_current = repair(initial_h_values) if parent exists else create_uniform_spread()\n      \n   Step 3: Anisotropic search\n      For each accepted move:\n        If local search (temperatures > 0.05):\n          Use L-BFGS-B for multiobjective nelder-mead with constraints h[i]\u2208[0,1] and sum(h)=target_sum\n        Else:\n          Use population-based covariance interpolation with progressive narrowing\n\n      Track:\n        best_global = None\n        last_improv_index = 0\n\n   Step 4: Adaptive mechanism\n      When stuck (no improvement in 10 candidates):\n        Insert structure from predefined intervals\n        - Select a starting index i\n        - Store (h[i], h[i+target_sum//4]) in interpolation buffer between 0.3 and 0.7\n        - Apply cubic interpolation for a 10-point patch\n\n   Step 5: Final stabilization\n      Repair candidate using Mode 2: ensure all containment\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\n   Default parameters:\n     n_points = 280 (as parent)\n     seed = provided\n     eval_budget = 1000 (adjust by time)\n     cooldown = 0.99\n     repair_mode_switch = 5e-3\n\n   Repair selection:\n     - Mode 1: Clip and scale\n       Sort indices by |i-center|, assign descending values, then scale to integral\n\n     - Mode 2: Nested clipping\n       1. Apply Mode 1\n       2. Any value >1\u21921, <0\u21920\n       3. Reapply Mode 1 while accounting for clamped sum\n\n   Fitness approximation:\n     Use RBF interpolation for unobserved lags, but validate top 10 shifts\n\n5. Compute budget/robustness:\n   - Dominant cost: FFT-based convolution for each evaluation\n   - Time per evaluation ~5ms per sample (cvxpy may use 10ms/lag)\n   - 100s budget \u2192 ~10M solutions\n   - Check temperature decay:\n        T=exponential(cooldown) while |log_improvements|>5\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n   - Check h[i] boundaries post-repair and sum post-repair\n   - Evaluate final candidate with metrics:\n        C5 global optimum search\n        Local validation via interpolate-shift-specialize on top candidates\n   - Return (best_h, final_c5, n_points) ensuring:\n        0.0 <= h[i] <= 1.0 for all i\n        abs(sum(h) - target_sum) < 1e-5\n        C5 < 0.38\n        Time used < budget_s\n\n   Validation function:\n        h_valid = repair(candidate, mode=2)\n        verify_integral(h_valid)\n        score = compute_c5(h_valid)\n        if score < 0.38 and abs(score_prev-best)>1e-5: \n            trigger_iso_search(score_prev)",
